  "sections": [
    {
      "h2": "Before you buy",
      "html": "<ul><li>Check the pattern’s suggested fabrics and the amount needed for your size and the fabric width.</li><li>Feel the drape: does it hang or hold its shape?</li><li>Check the fibre content and care label.</li><li><strong>Pre-wash</strong> washable fabrics before cutting to avoid shrinkage later.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig \"><img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1457972657980-4c9fddebec8d?w=1200&q=70&auto=format\" srcset=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1457972657980-4c9fddebec8d?w=700&q=70&auto=format 700w, https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1457972657980-4c9fddebec8d?w=1200&q=70&auto=format 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px\" alt=\"Pinning red fabric by hand\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\"><figcaption>Pre-wash, press and pin carefully before cutting.<span class=\"fig-credit\">Photo: <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/@krisatomic?utm_source=shmor&amp;utm_medium=referral\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Kris Atomic</a> / Unsplash</span></figcaption></figure>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Cotton",
      "html": "<p>Quilting cotton, poplin, lawn and chambray are the friendliest fabrics for beginners. Use a universal needle (80/12), all-purpose thread and a medium stitch length.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Linen",
      "html": "<p>Linen is strong, breathable and frays readily, so neaten seams with an overlocker, zigzag or French seams. It presses crisply with steam.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Jersey and knits",
      "html": "<p>Knits stretch, so use a <strong>ballpoint or stretch needle</strong>, a narrow zigzag or stretch stitch (or an overlocker), and don’t pull the fabric. A walking foot helps prevent wavy seams.</p><figure class=\"fig \"><img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1641320197434-6ae0ca235048?w=1200&q=70&auto=format\" srcset=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1641320197434-6ae0ca235048?w=700&q=70&auto=format 700w, https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1641320197434-6ae0ca235048?w=1200&q=70&auto=format 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px\" alt=\"Close-up of fabric being stitched on a sewing machine\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\"><figcaption>Use a stretch stitch or overlocker on jersey.<span class=\"fig-credit\">Photo: <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/@worsham?utm_source=shmor&amp;utm_medium=referral\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Ashley Diane Worsham</a> / Unsplash</span></figcaption></figure>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Denim and heavy fabrics",
      "html": "<p>Use a <strong>jeans needle</strong> (90/14 to 100/16), a longer stitch, and sew slowly over thick seams. A hump jumper or folded scrap helps the foot climb over bulky hems. Heavy-duty or industrial machines make light work of it.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Silk and satin",
      "html": "<p>Use a fine sharp needle, fine pins in the seam allowance and a short stitch. Tissue paper under the seam stops slippage and can be torn away afterwards.</p>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Lace and specialist fabrics",
      "html": "<p>Lace, velvet, sequins and faux leather all have their own tricks: a non-stick or walking foot, sharp new needles and plenty of testing on scraps.</p><div class=\"fig-pair\"><figure class=\"fig \"><img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1634225234360-7c921a9d2400?w=1200&q=70&auto=format\" srcset=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1634225234360-7c921a9d2400?w=700&q=70&auto=format 700w, https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1634225234360-7c921a9d2400?w=1200&q=70&auto=format 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px\" alt=\"White lace on a black background\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\"><figcaption>Lace needs fine needles and patience.<span class=\"fig-credit\">Photo: <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/@divazus?utm_source=shmor&amp;utm_medium=referral\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Divazus Fabric Store</a> / Unsplash</span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"fig \"><img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1628483211662-9bcc692c46dc?w=1200&q=70&auto=format\" srcset=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1628483211662-9bcc692c46dc?w=700&q=70&auto=format 700w, https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1628483211662-9bcc692c46dc?w=1200&q=70&auto=format 1200w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 760px\" alt=\"Leather wallet, thread and scissors\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\"><figcaption>Faux leather benefits from a non-stick or walking foot.<span class=\"fig-credit\">Photo: <a href=\"https://unsplash.com/@constantinevdokimov?utm_source=shmor&amp;utm_medium=referral\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Konstantin Evdokimov</a> / Unsplash</span></figcaption></figure></div>"
    },
    {
      "h2": "Getting your machine ready",
      "html": "<p>A freshly serviced machine with a new needle handles every fabric better. If you are in Leicestershire, <a href=\"http://www.pksm.co.uk/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">PK Sewing Machines</a> services domestic and industrial machines. Leicester itself, with <a href=\"/leicester-hosiery/\">its textile heritage</a>, is a great place to shop for fabric.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "faqs": [
    {
      "q": "What is the easiest fabric for beginners?",
      "a": "Medium-weight woven cotton, such as poplin or quilting cotton. It doesn’t stretch or slip and presses well."
    },
    {
      "q": "Do I need to pre-wash fabric?",
      "a": "For washable garments, yes. Washing before cutting means any shrinkage happens before you sew, not after."
    }
  ],
